1
00:00:08,484 --> 00:00:12,566
It is raining. And a question
comes, almost by itself.

2
00:00:12,646 --> 00:00:14,323
What is it, really?

3
00:00:15,136 --> 00:00:17,764
I am John Tan, known as Thusness.

4
00:00:17,844 --> 00:00:21,722
These are my own notes, from my
own practice and contemplation.

5
00:00:22,532 --> 00:00:25,867
In Section 2, I asked what
it is that appears at all.

6
00:00:25,947 --> 00:00:28,788
A sound, a colour, a thought.

7
00:00:28,868 --> 00:00:32,320
Each was vivid, not found,
and dependently arisen.

8
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:35,935
Near the end, mind and matter
turned up as two boxes,

9
00:00:36,015 --> 00:00:37,742
and neither box was found.

10
00:00:37,822 --> 00:00:40,762
This section takes up
mind and matter fully.

11
00:00:41,568 --> 00:00:46,125
But before going further, something
has to be seen. Not an argument.

12
00:00:46,205 --> 00:00:48,367
The mind that will hear every argument.

13
00:00:48,447 --> 00:00:52,715
If it is not seen first, everything
that follows will be heard through it.

14
00:00:52,795 --> 00:00:54,445
And nothing will change.

15
00:00:55,252 --> 00:00:59,809
So, the rain. The sound fills
the room, soft and steady.

16
00:00:59,889 --> 00:01:02,789
Now louder on the window. Now fading.

17
00:01:03,584 --> 00:01:05,261
What is it, really?

18
00:01:06,156 --> 00:01:08,336
Notice what kind of answer we want.

19
00:01:08,416 --> 00:01:10,224
Not "the sound of rain".

20
00:01:10,304 --> 00:01:13,580
That is only what appears,
and it does not satisfy.

21
00:01:13,660 --> 00:01:15,768
We want what it is made of underneath.

22
00:01:15,848 --> 00:01:17,697
What it comes down to in the end.

23
00:01:17,777 --> 00:01:20,283
We are looking for its
ultimate constituent.

24
00:01:21,088 --> 00:01:22,806
And the answers line up.

25
00:01:23,660 --> 00:01:29,006
Matter. It is really air moving,
water striking glass, nerves firing.

26
00:01:29,086 --> 00:01:31,714
The sound is how matter shows up to us.

27
00:01:32,520 --> 00:01:35,284
Mind. It is really consciousness.

28
00:01:35,364 --> 00:01:39,786
Whatever is out there, the sound
itself exists only as experienced.

29
00:01:40,588 --> 00:01:42,265
Or a third kind of stuff.

30
00:01:42,345 --> 00:01:45,621
It is really energy, vibration, a field.

31
00:01:45,701 --> 00:01:49,167
Or, in the older language
of China, it is qi.

32
00:01:49,247 --> 00:01:53,175
The Song dynasty thinker Zhang
Zai taught that all things are qi,

33
00:01:53,255 --> 00:01:58,343
condensing and dispersing, the way ice
forms from water and melts back into it.

34
00:01:59,144 --> 00:02:01,555
Each of these is held
by thoughtful people.

35
00:02:01,635 --> 00:02:03,620
And each starts from something true.

36
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:06,011
Sound does depend on air and ears.

37
00:02:06,091 --> 00:02:08,009
It is always experienced.

38
00:02:08,089 --> 00:02:09,911
It does involve vibration.

39
00:02:09,991 --> 00:02:12,198
I do not want to make any of them small.

40
00:02:12,996 --> 00:02:14,592
But look at what they share.

41
00:02:14,672 --> 00:02:18,396
Each takes the sound, and asks
for the something it is made of.

42
00:02:18,476 --> 00:02:22,092
And each stops only when it reaches
a stuff that is simply there.

43
00:02:22,172 --> 00:02:23,767
The bottom of the matter.

44
00:02:24,568 --> 00:02:28,922
To such a mind, the question cannot
rest until it finds what is ultimate.

45
00:02:29,002 --> 00:02:30,824
The sound comes and goes.

46
00:02:30,904 --> 00:02:32,957
Surely what it is made of does not.

47
00:02:33,037 --> 00:02:37,595
The world cannot just be happening, with
nothing underneath doing the happening.

48
00:02:38,396 --> 00:02:43,646
So it has to posit something.
A ground. A substrate. A stuff.

49
00:02:43,726 --> 00:02:46,595
The choice varies. The need does not.

50
00:02:46,675 --> 00:02:48,991
Surely, there has to be something.

51
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:51,654
And this is the important part.

52
00:02:51,734 --> 00:02:54,086
We do not experience this as a view.

53
00:02:54,166 --> 00:02:56,260
We take it as reality itself.

54
00:02:56,340 --> 00:02:58,094
The unquestionable default.

55
00:02:58,174 --> 00:03:01,871
Someone who says all is matter,
and someone who says all is mind,

56
00:03:01,951 --> 00:03:03,733
can argue for a lifetime.

57
00:03:03,812 --> 00:03:07,455
They never notice that they agree
on the one thing that matters most.

58
00:03:07,535 --> 00:03:09,086
That there must be a something.

59
00:03:09,166 --> 00:03:11,169
And the only question is which.

60
00:03:11,980 --> 00:03:13,874
Why does it feel so natural?

61
00:03:13,954 --> 00:03:17,167
Because the view is there
before any question is asked.

62
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:21,077
We start, without
noticing, from a worldview.

63
00:03:21,157 --> 00:03:24,977
There must be things, and things
must have fixed characteristics,

64
00:03:25,057 --> 00:03:26,498
and a nature of their own.

65
00:03:26,578 --> 00:03:30,561
And we are given a language that
presents the world exactly that way.

66
00:03:30,641 --> 00:03:35,724
A subject stands first, and a predicate
is said of it. The rose is red.

67
00:03:35,804 --> 00:03:38,228
A thing, with a colour attached.

68
00:03:39,036 --> 00:03:41,882
Nietzsche noticed that we
say the lightning flashes.

69
00:03:41,962 --> 00:03:46,324
As if the lightning were one thing, and
its flashing a second thing it does.

70
00:03:46,404 --> 00:03:48,679
Is there a lightning apart from the flash?

71
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:53,729
Even the rain is said this way.
It is raining. What is the it?

72
00:03:54,524 --> 00:03:59,122
I will not answer that. Here, the
asking matters more than any answer.

73
00:03:59,202 --> 00:04:02,510
Look at the question itself,
and at the way we ask it.

74
00:04:03,312 --> 00:04:07,217
Is it ever necessary to put it that
way, with an it in front of the raining?

75
00:04:08,020 --> 00:04:09,887
Why do we ask in such a manner?

76
00:04:09,967 --> 00:04:13,438
As if behind every happening,
there must be something doing it.

77
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:16,637
And must the answer always be a something?

78
00:04:17,436 --> 00:04:20,513
Stay with these, before
reaching for a reply.

79
00:04:20,593 --> 00:04:22,469
Most of us have never asked them.

80
00:04:22,549 --> 00:04:25,992
Because the grammar asked
for us. And answered too.

81
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:30,375
Growing up inside that grammar,
we are moulded to think that way,

82
00:04:30,455 --> 00:04:33,803
to analyse that way, and to
orient ourselves that way.

83
00:04:33,883 --> 00:04:37,988
To analyse is to break things into
parts, each with its own nature.

84
00:04:38,068 --> 00:04:41,656
To explain is to find the thing
underneath that does the producing.

85
00:04:41,736 --> 00:04:45,710
To orient is to look behind what
appears, for what is really there.

86
00:04:46,508 --> 00:04:48,674
None of this means giving language up.

87
00:04:48,754 --> 00:04:50,930
The Buddha still said I and you.

88
00:04:51,010 --> 00:04:54,354
I still say the rose
is red. The words work.

89
00:04:54,434 --> 00:04:57,913
What has to change is that they
no longer mould what is seen.

90
00:04:57,993 --> 00:05:00,825
They can be used, without being believed.

91
00:05:01,632 --> 00:05:06,434
So, before going further, this must
be recognised, and clearly seen.

92
00:05:06,514 --> 00:05:09,722
Not believed, or disbelieved. Seen.

93
00:05:09,802 --> 00:05:12,113
The way you see a pair of tinted glasses,

94
00:05:12,193 --> 00:05:13,898
once you notice they are on.

95
00:05:14,692 --> 00:05:18,366
If it is not seen, every step
will be heard in the old grammar.

96
00:05:18,446 --> 00:05:21,192
Emptiness will sound
like a new kind of stuff.

97
00:05:21,272 --> 00:05:24,005
The final answer to "what is it, really?"

98
00:05:24,085 --> 00:05:27,338
The argument will seem
clever, and change nothing.

99
00:05:28,136 --> 00:05:31,983
Here, Buddhism, and the Middle
Way of Nāgārjuna above all,

100
00:05:32,063 --> 00:05:34,338
does something I find completely new.

101
00:05:35,148 --> 00:05:39,674
Nearly every philosophy, East
and West, accepts the question,

102
00:05:39,754 --> 00:05:45,412
what is it really, and competes on
the answer. Matter. Mind. Energy.

103
00:05:45,492 --> 00:05:47,206
God. The One.

104
00:05:47,286 --> 00:05:49,203
They disagree about the something.

105
00:05:49,283 --> 00:05:51,259
They never doubt there must be one.

106
00:05:52,072 --> 00:05:54,578
The Middle Way does not join the contest.

107
00:05:54,658 --> 00:05:56,294
It turns to the question.

108
00:05:57,092 --> 00:05:59,068
It offers no rival something.

109
00:05:59,148 --> 00:06:03,294
Nāgārjuna wrote: if I had a
thesis, that fault would be mine.

110
00:06:03,374 --> 00:06:06,160
Since I have no thesis,
I am without fault.

111
00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:10,277
As I read him, he holds no thesis
about what things ultimately are.

112
00:06:10,357 --> 00:06:14,290
Because the search for such a thing
is exactly what he is examining.

113
00:06:15,096 --> 00:06:17,751
It examines the something
on its own terms.

114
00:06:17,831 --> 00:06:20,360
It does not set one view against another.

115
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:23,730
It takes the premises the
other person already holds,

116
00:06:23,810 --> 00:06:27,131
follows them through, and
shows that they cannot stand.

117
00:06:27,940 --> 00:06:29,495
It changes the question.

118
00:06:29,575 --> 00:06:31,383
Not, what is it made of?

119
00:06:31,463 --> 00:06:35,369
But, dependent on what does
this arise, and how is it named?

120
00:06:36,176 --> 00:06:38,519
It does not make emptiness the new answer.

121
00:06:38,599 --> 00:06:41,114
Emptiness is not what things are made of.

122
00:06:41,194 --> 00:06:44,130
It is the absence of what
the question was looking for.

123
00:06:44,210 --> 00:06:47,636
Nāgārjuna warns that
emptiness, wrongly grasped,

124
00:06:47,716 --> 00:06:50,303
harms like a snake picked
up by the wrong end.

125
00:06:51,108 --> 00:06:54,293
And it keeps the world.
The rain still falls.

126
00:06:54,373 --> 00:06:56,182
The umbrella still works.

127
00:06:56,262 --> 00:06:58,442
None of it needs a something underneath.

128
00:06:59,248 --> 00:07:02,365
Here I part from one way the
Middle Way is often read.

129
00:07:02,445 --> 00:07:06,577
As endless negation, taking everything
apart until nothing is left.

130
00:07:06,657 --> 00:07:08,248
That is not how I see it.

131
00:07:08,328 --> 00:07:10,816
Nothing is denied that is actually met.

132
00:07:10,896 --> 00:07:14,295
What falls away is only the
something the question demanded.

133
00:07:14,375 --> 00:07:16,351
And with it, the demand.

134
00:07:17,156 --> 00:07:19,947
So let me take the
default apart, a little.

135
00:07:20,027 --> 00:07:22,026
This is not seen in one stroke.

136
00:07:22,106 --> 00:07:23,697
It is seen gradually.

137
00:07:23,777 --> 00:07:26,061
But the shape of what is found is simple.

138
00:07:26,141 --> 00:07:27,964
The default fails twice.

139
00:07:28,044 --> 00:07:29,825
Once against experience.

140
00:07:29,905 --> 00:07:31,596
And once against itself.

141
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:37,406
First, experience. Go back to
the rain. What is actually met?

142
00:07:37,486 --> 00:07:41,224
The sound, soft, then louder, then fading.

143
00:07:41,304 --> 00:07:44,186
The coolness at the
window. The grey light.

144
00:07:44,266 --> 00:07:46,373
A thought: it is raining.

145
00:07:46,453 --> 00:07:49,675
Each one arises, is vivid, and is gone.

146
00:07:49,755 --> 00:07:51,514
And the next one is fresh.

147
00:07:52,324 --> 00:07:58,009
Where, in all of this, is the stuff it
is made of? It is never met. Not once.

148
00:07:58,089 --> 00:08:02,167
Matter as a stuff, mind as
a stuff, energy as a stuff.

149
00:08:02,247 --> 00:08:07,371
Each is always one step behind what
appears. Inferred. Never found.

150
00:08:07,451 --> 00:08:10,767
What is met is always the
changing, dependent happening.

151
00:08:10,847 --> 00:08:13,661
What is posited is always the unchanging,

152
00:08:13,741 --> 00:08:15,564
independent something underneath it.

153
00:08:15,644 --> 00:08:20,011
The default asks us to take as most
real the one thing that never appears.

154
00:08:20,816 --> 00:08:23,349
Second, the default against itself.

155
00:08:23,429 --> 00:08:25,210
It was not made up from nothing.

156
00:08:25,290 --> 00:08:28,512
It was derived, from
premises that seem obvious.

157
00:08:28,592 --> 00:08:32,131
Take those premises seriously,
and follow them through.

158
00:08:32,940 --> 00:08:34,481
The first premise.

159
00:08:34,561 --> 00:08:38,788
The real is what is left when
analysis ends. Then analyse.

160
00:08:38,868 --> 00:08:42,185
The table comes down to
wood. Wood to molecules.

161
00:08:42,265 --> 00:08:43,924
Molecules to atoms.

162
00:08:44,004 --> 00:08:45,663
Atoms to particles.

163
00:08:45,743 --> 00:08:47,307
Particles to fields.

164
00:08:47,387 --> 00:08:49,345
Each floor has a floor below.

165
00:08:49,425 --> 00:08:54,305
Vasubandhu asked of the smallest
atom: if it has sides, it has parts.

166
00:08:54,385 --> 00:08:57,158
If it has no sides, nothing can touch it,

167
00:08:57,238 --> 00:09:00,405
and nothing can be built
from it. Mind fares the same.

168
00:09:00,485 --> 00:09:03,177
A moment of mind comes
down to shorter moments,

169
00:09:03,257 --> 00:09:05,555
with no partless instant at the bottom.

170
00:09:05,635 --> 00:09:09,549
And energy, field and qi are
each known only by what they do.

171
00:09:09,629 --> 00:09:14,064
A stuff known only by its relations
is not a stuff standing on its own.

172
00:09:14,872 --> 00:09:16,400
The second premise.

173
00:09:16,480 --> 00:09:20,109
Characteristics need a
bearer. Then find the bearer.

174
00:09:20,189 --> 00:09:22,459
Strip away every characteristic.

175
00:09:22,539 --> 00:09:27,160
Colour, shape, weight, warmth.
What is left to bear them?

176
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:28,791
Nothing can be said of it.

177
00:09:28,871 --> 00:09:30,421
Not even that it is there.

178
00:09:30,501 --> 00:09:34,565
Leave it with its characteristics,
and it is no longer the bare bearer.

179
00:09:34,645 --> 00:09:36,635
Only more characteristics.

180
00:09:37,436 --> 00:09:41,681
The third premise. The ground must
be independent and unchanging.

181
00:09:41,761 --> 00:09:43,542
That is what makes it a ground.

182
00:09:43,622 --> 00:09:46,124
But look at the job it was posited to do.

183
00:09:46,204 --> 00:09:48,773
It was meant to explain
a world that changes,

184
00:09:48,853 --> 00:09:50,553
arises and passes.

185
00:09:50,633 --> 00:09:53,991
Something truly unchanging
cannot give rise to anything.

186
00:09:54,071 --> 00:09:56,273
If it did, it would change.

187
00:09:56,353 --> 00:09:59,493
And something truly independent
cannot even be known.

188
00:09:59,574 --> 00:10:02,523
Because to be known is
already to stand in relation.

189
00:10:02,603 --> 00:10:05,993
The ground cannot do the one
thing it was posited for.

190
00:10:06,792 --> 00:10:10,303
So the default is not only
unfound in experience.

191
00:10:10,383 --> 00:10:13,877
Analysed on its own premises,
it is contradictory,

192
00:10:13,957 --> 00:10:16,041
illogical, and untenable.

193
00:10:16,852 --> 00:10:20,798
What, then, is it? Not reality. A habit.

194
00:10:20,878 --> 00:10:23,533
A habitual way of
understanding a happening.

195
00:10:24,344 --> 00:10:29,662
A sound happens. The habit supplies
something that sounds. A flash happens.

196
00:10:29,742 --> 00:10:33,901
The habit supplies the lightning
that flashes. A thought happens.

197
00:10:33,981 --> 00:10:36,279
The habit supplies the mind that has it.

198
00:10:36,359 --> 00:10:40,776
And because the habit is old,
shared, and built into how we speak,

199
00:10:40,856 --> 00:10:42,737
it feels like the way things are.

200
00:10:43,548 --> 00:10:49,355
Two cautions. This is not "nothing is
there". The rain is heard. It is wet.

201
00:10:49,435 --> 00:10:51,000
The window is cold.

202
00:10:51,080 --> 00:10:53,730
You take an umbrella, and you stay dry.

203
00:10:53,810 --> 00:10:58,232
What is not found is only the something
underneath. Never the appearing.

204
00:10:59,032 --> 00:11:04,568
And nothing replaces the something.
Not mind. Not awareness. Not energy.

205
00:11:04,648 --> 00:11:06,823
Not emptiness as a finer stuff.

206
00:11:06,903 --> 00:11:10,877
To swap one ground for another
is the same habit, still at work.

207
00:11:11,684 --> 00:11:15,694
When the habit is seen for what it is, the
insistence that there has to be something

208
00:11:15,774 --> 00:11:19,068
begins to loosen. Not
because an argument has won.

209
00:11:19,148 --> 00:11:21,989
Because it is seen that the
question, what is it really,

210
00:11:22,069 --> 00:11:24,724
was asking for something
that was never needed.

211
00:11:25,536 --> 00:11:29,550
This is Section 3, Part 1 of
the Dependent Arising series.

212
00:11:30,364 --> 00:11:32,503
The rain was only ever raining.

